msgid "Analog Input Pins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:7
#: dc68f3a1e03d435c8b20239cdc77c365
msgid "In addition to digital input and output pins, autopilots have analog input pins that allow measuring voltages precisely. These are commonly used for the power monitor voltge and current sense inputs, but other pins are sometimes provided for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:9
#: 8535f6e060a94ff7836454af5a4d2d24
msgid "RSSI (Received Signal Strength Input)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:10
#: a09e7677cf3f4cd9a4adf92649ce7f3e
msgid "Analog Airspeed Sensor Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:11
#: 3dc985ab29ce4e249ed2fd25b8fd4660
msgid "Analog Fuel Level Sensor Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:12
#: 57e99fbda3154d1e8fb83e34471c5906
msgid "Analog Sonar/Rangefinder Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:13
#: 75b4e6cfeef3451591e71f5e26d68c58
msgid "Analog Temperature Sensor Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:15
#: bf717f0395d3410cb5caafc0008a6034
msgid "All pins can accept 0-3.3v inputs. Unless the documentation (OEM or Wiki) specifically specifies 6.6V input range, only apply 3.3 maximum!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:17
#: 662cdba8668b45bbaee53a2f3e826fb6
msgid "When any of these inputs are enabled by the appropriate sensor type selection, a ``_PIN`` parameter will need to be entered to designate which \"pin\" on the autopilot is to be used. Often, the correct pin number for the autopilot's analog inputs will be documented either on its Wiki page here, or the OEM's documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:19
#: 5ffc370c7b1b46dbb543a21283b9e45b
msgid "If not, then examining the autopilot's ``hwdef.dat`` file `here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef>`__ can provide the information. The process is a bit difficult but manageable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:21
#: ed1c2ddbd6534d28838c4b12093c19a3
msgid "For example, the `CUAV-X7 autopilot hwdef.dat <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/CUAV-X7/hwdef.dat>`__ has a section designating its internal A-to-D converters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:44
#: a924300d30b24902bca5ce870fa0300e
msgid "The last three lines define inputs used internally on the board to monitor various board supply voltages. The first two lines define the voltage and current sense inputs, the next define user analog inputs and the RSSI input. In order to determine which pins numbers are used in ArduPilot parameters, one more lookup step is required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:46
#: 5695e90e7dc342b2becdda6043d1663e
msgid "After determining which cpu is used in the autopilot, the pin numbers corresponding to the cpu pins can be determined from the `cpu's definition table here <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/scripts>`__. In the above example, the cpu is STM32H743, and looking at the bottom of its `definition file <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/scripts/STM32H743xx.py>`__, you can find its cpu to ardupilot pin tables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-analog-pins.rst:73
#: 0a1d8732db9148ba8c208dd01b8fddd5
msgid "and for ADC1, the power monitor voltage input, PA0, would be ArduPilot pin \"16\", the RSSI input, PF12, would correspond to ArduPilot pin \"6\", etc. and these pin values would be used in the appropriate ``_PIN`` parameter."
msgstr ""
